<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-asia</id><updated>2026-11-23T20:23:40Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-asia" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-12758?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-asia" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Tajikistan follows US call, withdraws from ICC</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3ddbdeb423f62d078085230b8d9dade83c3f0bcf370edbe173b6558295d33f4e</id><updated>2026-11-23T20:22:45Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T18:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/tajikistan-follows-us-call-withdraws-from-icc/a-80023903--9937f6abaec0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/tajikistan-follows-us-call-withdraws-from-icc/a-80023903?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Tajikistan has initiated its withdrawal from the International Criminal Court as the US calls for it to be "dismantled." The decision was made during a recent visit from Russian President Vladimir Putin.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>After Japan's APEC snub, what's next for its China ties?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0cb43eb42af3c74347cd814f359b0bda446fc109fb0b35fd9cf43eb600ac0b6f</id><updated>2026-11-23T20:22:55Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T15:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/after-japan-s-apec-snub-what-s-next-for-its-china-ties/a-80020823--0940c063c8fc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/after-japan-s-apec-snub-what-s-next-for-its-china-ties/a-80020823?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Japan has long-running concerns over Chinese military expansionism, and Beijing has bristled at Sanae Takaichi's comments on Taiwan. The frosty ties were on full display at the APEC summit.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Gukesh to defend chess crown against rising star Sindarov</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7ed9c9702cfecbb22928fd12d689b5046f212483b9eadef16d263a46d989b815</id><updated>2026-11-23T20:22:58Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T15:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/gukesh-to-defend-chess-crown-against-rising-star-sindarov/a-80021806--07e5204aa07f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/gukesh-to-defend-chess-crown-against-rising-star-sindarov/a-80021806?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As the World Chess championship gets underway, it's no coincidence that the titleholder, Gukesh Dommaraju, and his challenger, Jakhovir Sindarov, are both from Asia.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Nepal's new PM eyes closer ties with India amid lingering disputes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bbe211b9253ff67a4328674aaf8e236e15f44463b7277752cc95f64c91acc248</id><updated>2026-11-23T20:23:01Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T14:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nepal-s-new-pm-eyes-closer-ties-with-india-amid-lingering-disputes/a-80021769--65c0c20879de.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nepal-s-new-pm-eyes-closer-ties-with-india-amid-lingering-disputes/a-80021769?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">On his first foreign bilateral visit, rapper-turned-Prime Minister Balendra Shah sought deeper ties with Nepal's neighbor and largest trading partner, while steering clear of sticky territorial issues.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Nvidia reinstates former CEO Jensen Huang despite China espionage scandal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e979c10604939c7955ed9c29f2acb7fdec56f61e17f540c1d7554c36ddb0c3e4</id><updated>2026-11-23T20:23:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T14:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nvidia-reinstates-former-ceo-jensen-huang-despite-china-espionage-scandal/a-80021926--88659c21678b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nvidia-reinstates-former-ceo-jensen-huang-despite-china-espionage-scandal/a-80021926?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Nvidia's board voted unanimously to bring back the disgraced CEO, who resigned this month amid news of his affairs. He's suspected of having had a relationship with a Chinese intelligence asset.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>China, ASEAN countries struggle over South China Sea code of conduct</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b6a64eeab7b0ea652d9e38b8bd4da2c98b9442a5ec79acf130136a28e7529986</id><updated>2026-11-23T20:22:17Z</updated><published>2026-11-22T08:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/china-asean-countries-struggle-over-south-china-sea-code-of-conduct/a-80009799--a3492edf3810.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/china-asean-countries-struggle-over-south-china-sea-code-of-conduct/a-80009799?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Philippines wanted a South China Sea code of conduct in place by 2026. But persistent disagreements between China and ASEAN countries are slowing progress toward a deal.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>India: Nepal PM Balendra Shah heads to Delhi for first bilateral visit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6f7e2ff32467325b702057d0e19306a60ea036d6c9326d0fac05345fe5707473</id><updated>2026-11-23T20:22:17Z</updated><published>2026-11-22T07:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-nepal-pm-balendra-shah-heads-to-delhi-for-first-bilateral-visit/live-80008104--4f17524b4e9e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-nepal-pm-balendra-shah-heads-to-delhi-for-first-bilateral-visit/live-80008104?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Nepal's rapper-turned-prime minister Balendra Shah is in New Delhi for his first foreign bilateral trip since taking office. He is expected to discuss flood recovery, trade and energy in his talks with Modi. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Dozens missing as deadly fire tears through Indonesian candy factory</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:53989d3139d3dc60a7d8fcb454d7633171461a041f90664bf103f2b8308da8bc</id><updated>2026-11-23T20:23:40Z</updated><published>2026-11-22T06:14:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/dozens-missing-as-deadly-fire-tears-through-indonesian-candy-factory/a-80012342--200c1388a684.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/dozens-missing-as-deadly-fire-tears-through-indonesian-candy-factory/a-80012342?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">At least 24 people were killed in a devastating fire at a confectionery factory on Java. Officials said many more people remain unaccounted for, prompting fears of a much larger tragedy.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>FIFA presidential election 2027: Infantino facing Diallo and Tashima — could an alliance change everything?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b5d9b6125e17cd56fed8a63c7ad246e37603a64e80263920b52a1073cd3a2152</id><updated>2026-11-23T20:22:17Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T12:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/fifa-presidential-election-2027-infantino-facing-diallo-and-tashima-could-an-alliance-change-everyth/a-80002882--01040a665cff.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/fifa-presidential-election-2027-infantino-facing-diallo-and-tashima-could-an-alliance-change-everything/a-80002882?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Two challengers to Gianni Infantino have registered for next year's FIFA presidential election. What do Philippe Diallo and Kozo Tashima stand for – and do they stand a chance against the incumbent?</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Pakistan minister to visit India, but no breakthrough expected</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bbad263e975361b7896f254012d1320aaf7ca81c01983c492315e060ecb5ce60</id><updated>2026-11-23T20:22:17Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T13:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/pakistan-minister-to-visit-india-but-no-breakthrough-expected/a-79991717--07503556e8b2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/pakistan-minister-to-visit-india-but-no-breakthrough-expected/a-79991717?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A Pakistani minister's visit to India for a Shanghai Cooperation Organization forum marks a rare high-level contact between the two archrivals, but analysts say it does not signal a resumption of bilateral engagement.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Iran's growing exodus of young talent</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:04fc1230a9b4b6eccf5b28998471636109e173b8673d5ef0e25549390734ac5f</id><updated>2026-11-23T20:22:17Z</updated><published>2026-11-17T16:36:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-s-growing-exodus-of-young-talent/a-79960368--aa300b774c88.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-s-growing-exodus-of-young-talent/a-79960368?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Conflict and uncertainty are driving more and more educated young Iranians to consider leaving the country.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
